── detail · found in /work/acme/.mcp.json ──
radar found a Jira site in /work/acme/.mcp.json. Do you want to use it?

FOUND
gamma.atlassian.net  the site's address, as written
JIRA_EMAIL           the account

radar stores only the variables' names (env:NAME) and reads their values each time it starts. It never shows the values or saves them.

It is the file's "tools" entry. It also watches GAM (acceptance criteria in customfield_10044). Its token is typed into the file: radar does not copy it, and asks which variable holds it.

IF YOU USE IT
radar adds the site gamma and asks which variable holds its token.

⏎ uses it

§ :site: SITE
  The address you use for Jira, like ankh-morpork.atlassian.net.
  Paste any Jira link; radar keeps the site part.
§ :person: EMAIL
  The email you sign in to Atlassian with, on your profile:
  id.atlassian.com / profile
§ :connection: API TOKEN  about a minute
  1 Open Atlassian's API token page:
  id.atlassian.com / api tokens   open · copy
  2 Create API token, label it radar, pick an expiry, then Create.
  3 Copy it now: Atlassian shows it once. Paste it into token, or:
  $ export JIRA_TOKEN=…
  then the token is env:JIRA_TOKEN
§ :warning: IF IT IS REFUSED
  401: the email and token don't match, or the token expired.
  Company login (SSO)? An API token still works; ask your admin if API tokens are switched off.
§ :link: MORE
  Atlassian: manage API tokens
  radar guide: connect Jira
